@baseUrl=http://localhost:8000/api/v1/participants
@poolParticipantId=REPLACE_WITH_POOL_PARTICIPANT_ID
@poolId=REPLACE_WITH_POOL_ID
@paymentId=REPLACE_WITH_PAYMENT_ID
@addressId=REPLACE_WITH_RETAILER_OWN_ADDRESS_ID
@accessToken=REPLACE_WITH_RETAILER_ACCESS_TOKEN

# See 00-smooth-flow.http for a chained run that creates a real pool/
# payment/address/token end to end instead of hand-editing the
# placeholders above. Note address_ref must be one of the caller's own
# addresses (checked server-side) — it can't just be any address id.

### create poolParticipant (RETAILER only — user_ref is derived from the token, not sent)

POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
    "pool_ref": "{{poolId}}",
    "payment_ref": "{{paymentId}}",
    "address_ref": "{{addressId}}",
    "quantity": 15
}

### list poolParticipants (ADMIN sees all; anyone else only their own)

GET {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### list poolParticipants for a given pool (ADMIN use case: see everyone in a pool)

GET {{baseUrl}}?pool_ref={{poolId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### get poolParticipant by id

GET {{baseUrl}}/{{poolParticipantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### update poolParticipant (RETAILER, own participant only, only while the pool is still OPEN)

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/{{poolParticipantId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
    "quantity": 12
}

### delete poolParticipant (RETAILER, own participant only — pool OPEN, COMPLETED, or CANCELLED 7+ days ago)

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{poolParticipantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}